# Link what you name: always apply

Before you write or rewrite any of these, read and apply
[`linking-references`](../skills/linking-references/SKILL.md):

- A pull request body, or a commit message body.
- A review comment, a review summary, or a reply to review feedback.
- A ticket description or comment.
- A chat message.
- A written answer to an engineer or to the user, including a chat answer and a progress update.
- A committed document.

## Forbidden

- A bare ticket key, pull request number, repository name, or "the doc" at its first mention, on a
  surface that does not link it for you. A code span around it is still bare.
- A URL that you did not resolve from a source: a guessed number, a guessed path, or a guessed
  route.
- "here", "this link", or a raw URL as the link text.
